# Generated import aggregators (`scripts/mk_all.py`) are sorted lists of one-line imports: each
# library root and its per-directory shards under `<root>/All/`. (The test library has no
# aggregator: Lake builds it from a glob, see `lakefile.toml`.) Union merge lets a local
# `git merge` combine concurrent additions in the same neighbourhood; `mk_all --check` in CI
# still enforces the canonical content. GitHub ignores merge drivers, so on GitHub such
# additions conflict; the shards confine that to additions in the same directory.
Complexity.lean merge=union
Complexity/All/** merge=union
abstracts/ComplexityAbstracts.lean merge=union
# `references.bib` names the opt-in local driver of `scripts/resolve_bib_conflict.py`, which merges
# entries by key. Where `merge.bibkeys.driver` is not configured, git uses its ordinary text merge.
references.bib merge=bibkeys
